Original commit body from 0b0cd9adcf04f2e576bab32f6ac268b50722dc3d:

A node id now has its own type, `NodeId`, so mypy rejects an id that was not built by an id factory.

## Why

Node ids follow one grammar (`language:path:lines:name:kind`), written by a small set of factory functions. An id assembled by hand with an f-string can leave that grammar without any test noticing; `scripts/check-id-construction` catches the f-string at pre-commit, but nothing checked the value's path through the code. With a distinct type, a plain `str` reaching an id field is a type error that the strict mypy ratchet counts.

## What changed

- `NodeId = NewType("NodeId", str)` in `ir.py`. The factories (`make_symbol_id`, `make_file_id`, `make_module_import_dst`, the external-id helper) return it.
- `Symbol.id`, `UsageContext.symbol_ref` and `DataModel.symbol_id` are typed `NodeId`.
- Two ways a `str` becomes a `NodeId` outside the factories: `read_node_id` (one call: a dangling edge endpoint in file-id shape becomes the file node it names) and `relativize_node_id` (the repo-root strip at finalize).
- Thirteen hand-built ids whose text a factory reproduces byte for byte now go through the factory.
- Six producers whose hand-built id differs from what a factory would emit keep their text and wrap it at the site. Each is listed with its reason in `test_id_newtypes.py`: event names, template file names, handlebars partials, bibtex keys, blade view names, and rust-analyzer's in-place kind rewrite.
- `scripts/check-id-construction` sees through `NodeId(...)` and `read_node_id(...)`.
- `test_id_newtypes.py` pins the typed fields and three tables: every place that mints an id (11), every hand-built wrap (6), every boundary read (1). Dropping any one of the 18 entries fails a test (checked one at a time).

## Left as `str`, with the reason

- `Edge.dst`: a dst is a node id or an unresolved reference that finalize turns into a boundary node. 67 producer sites write it as an f-string; 12 are outside the node-id grammar and 34 interpolate a name that may hold `:`.
- `Edge.src`: `tests/test_rct_public_api_pinned.py` pins its type as `str` and asks for coordination first, and 11 producer sites plus the SCIP builders' no-resolver path write a src that is not a node id.

Owner ruling 2026-11-16: typing `Edge.src` and fixing the six wrapped producers are follow-up items, filed after this merges.

